<!DOCTYPE template>
<!--
  Description:
    Per-deck timecode signal status. Read-only.

    This is the piece no existing Mixxx skin provides. Every community small-screen
    skin is a controller companion built for jog wheels and pads, so none surfaces
    vinyl control state. On a DVS appliance this is the only troubleshooting surface
    for the timecode path: nothing on the mixer or the turntables reports whether
    Mixxx is actually reading the control signal.

    Only the *status* lives here. The vinyl on/off, mode (ABS/REL/CONST) and
    passthrough controls are deliberately NOT on screen - they are set-once mode
    switches, they are bound to the DJM-T1's own buttons in the controller mapping,
    and the deck info row has no horizontal room for them at 1024px anyway. Controls
    on hardware, state on screen.

    Values come from src/vinylcontrol/defs_vinylcontrol.h:
      0 VINYL_STATUS_DISABLED   vinyl control is off for this deck
      1 VINYL_STATUS_OK         timecode locked and tracking
      2 VINYL_STATUS_WARNING    signal degraded - dirty stylus, low level, worn record
      3 VINYL_STATUS_ERROR      no usable timecode

    Rendered as coloured text rather than pixmaps so it needs no new image assets
    and stays readable at arm's length on a small panel.

  Variables:
    channel: the deck number, e.g. 1
-->
<Template>
  <PushButton>
    <ObjectName>DvsStatusLight</ObjectName>
    <Tooltip>Timecode signal status for this deck.

OFF  - vinyl control disabled
OK   - timecode locked and tracking
WARN - signal degraded (stylus, level, worn record)
ERR  - no usable timecode</Tooltip>
    <Size>76f,26f</Size>
    <NumberStates>4</NumberStates>
    <State>
      <Number>0</Number>
      <Text>OFF</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>1</Number>
      <Text>OK</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>2</Number>
      <Text>WARN</Text>
    </State>
    <State>
      <Number>3</Number>
      <Text>ERR</Text>
    </State>
    <!-- displayValue only: no ButtonState connection, so there is no control for a
         stray touch to write to and the widget is inert. -->
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],vinylcontrol_status</ConfigKey>
      <BindProperty>displayValue</BindProperty>
    </Connection>
  </PushButton>
</Template>
